WEBVTT

00:13.840 --> 00:14.870
What's wrong?

00:16.870 --> 00:21.870
Tomorrow's soirée is our last one 
before graduation, isn't it?

00:22.340 --> 00:24.420
It is. Why?

00:24.420 --> 00:30.340
I'm truly honored that you'll 
be the one escorting me...

00:30.340 --> 00:33.040
But are you sure it's all right?

00:34.570 --> 00:35.510
Euphyllia, eh?

00:37.720 --> 00:40.070
You don't need to worry about a thing.

00:40.070 --> 00:43.140
Just let me take care of everything 
when it comes to her.

00:43.140 --> 00:44.590
Yes, but...

00:45.170 --> 00:50.190
I'm sorry. I don't fully understand 
the rules and etiquette of nobility.

00:50.480 --> 00:55.920
Because you lived as a commoner before 
Baron Cyan took you in as his daughter?

00:56.660 --> 00:57.350
Yes.

01:09.780 --> 01:12.020
After my mother died,

01:12.020 --> 01:14.460
I was taken in by an orphanage.

01:18.610 --> 01:21.670
But... it didn't work out very well.

01:22.250 --> 01:24.380
People kept making strange passes at me,

01:24.820 --> 01:26.930
or just plain bullying me...

01:27.670 --> 01:30.860
so I've never been very good 
at interacting with people.

01:33.070 --> 01:35.820
Rejecting and failing to understand 
someone alien to you...

01:36.380 --> 01:39.730
The disconnect between 
commoners and nobles...

01:40.220 --> 01:42.940
This kingdom has become quite warped.

01:47.990 --> 01:51.090
I want to change the Kingdom of Palettia.

01:52.030 --> 01:54.530
I know you can do it, Prince Algard!

01:54.530 --> 01:56.550
You can become a great king!

01:57.790 --> 02:02.610
The previous king, my grandfather, 
tried to change the kingdom, too.

02:03.480 --> 02:04.750
But he failed.

02:05.350 --> 02:09.470
With a half-hearted approach, 
it would be impossible.

02:23.300 --> 02:25.860
The road ahead of us will be a bumpy one.

02:26.340 --> 02:28.580
Some unfortunate things might happen.

02:28.770 --> 02:29.760
Despite that...

02:30.260 --> 02:32.500
Will you still stay with me, Lainie?

02:33.210 --> 02:33.990
Yes!

02:46.620 --> 02:48.270
Prince Algard...

04:11.520 --> 04:19.980
The Magical Revolution

04:11.520 --> 04:19.980
The Magical Revolution

04:11.520 --> 04:19.980
of the Reincarnated Princess and the Genius Young Lady

04:27.320 --> 04:28.420
Miss Lainie.

04:29.710 --> 04:31.630
Do you not intend to drink your tea?

04:31.630 --> 04:34.280
Oh... I-I'm sorry.

04:36.860 --> 04:41.030
I'm... a vampire, aren't I?

04:45.920 --> 04:48.980
And the only reason so many 
people have been kind to me

04:48.980 --> 04:51.380
is because I charmed them 
without knowing it.

04:53.350 --> 04:57.810
And yet, Miss Anis and her friends 
treat me so well.

04:59.930 --> 05:03.120
If you fret too much, 
happiness will escape you.

05:03.120 --> 05:04.290
But...

05:05.370 --> 05:09.030
The more complicated a problem is, 
the longer it persists.

05:09.520 --> 05:13.770
But putting that aside, there is one problem 
that you can resolve here and now.

05:13.770 --> 05:15.000
What is it?

05:15.490 --> 05:19.710
A maid's concern that the excellent tea 
she brewed will go cold.

05:26.040 --> 05:28.350
Right. Thank you.

05:32.730 --> 05:34.070
It is indeed excellent.

05:34.070 --> 05:36.050
You honor me with your praise.

05:48.160 --> 05:49.080
Miss Il—

05:49.360 --> 05:50.540
Quiet.

05:53.780 --> 05:58.510
Remain calm and listen to me. 
Someone just infiltrated the villa.

06:12.970 --> 06:15.420
H-How could there be an intruder?

06:15.770 --> 06:20.650
It's all right. Miss Anis will fly here 
in response to the alarm immediately.

06:20.650 --> 06:24.360
B-But Miss Anis left to speak before 
the Ministry of the Arcane...

06:26.780 --> 06:30.500
Yes, which is why we should 
take refuge at the castle.

06:30.940 --> 06:34.190
I can find my way around 
the villa with my eyes closed.

06:38.650 --> 06:39.830
Miss Lainie! That fog!

06:39.830 --> 06:42.160
It might be poisonous! Don't inhale it!

06:42.810 --> 06:45.490
We'll leave through the window! 
Hold on tight!

06:52.130 --> 06:54.520
As always, you do make quick judgments,

06:54.520 --> 06:56.530
but you have a problem following through.

07:03.150 --> 07:04.380
Fire Arrow!

07:09.930 --> 07:11.150
Miss Ilia!

07:18.880 --> 07:20.210
Why...

07:23.170 --> 07:26.990
I won't apologize, 
nor will I beg for forgiveness.

07:26.990 --> 07:27.620
But...

07:29.090 --> 07:31.340
It is unfortunate, Lainie.

07:40.000 --> 07:43.520
With regard to the speech 
by Duke Magenta's daughter,

07:43.520 --> 07:47.480
as head of the Ministry of the Arcane, 
I would like to stress one additional point.

07:47.480 --> 07:51.200
Spirit contracts are the very 
foundation of our kingdom!

07:51.650 --> 07:54.590
This was because our first 
king established this kingdom

07:54.590 --> 07:58.340
by forging a direct contract 
with a greater spirit.

07:58.340 --> 08:00.120
<i>I wanna go home...</i>

08:00.120 --> 08:01.780
Princess Anisphia.

08:02.510 --> 08:05.750
The lecture you gave was magnificent.

08:05.750 --> 08:07.580
Uh, thanks...

08:07.880 --> 08:09.800
<i>And who are you? I'm lost here.</i>

08:10.070 --> 08:12.560
I am Moritz Chartreuse.

08:12.560 --> 08:15.090
<i>He's the son of that old 
geezer at the lecture!</i>

08:15.090 --> 08:16.710
<i>And one of Al's flunkies, at that!</i>

08:16.910 --> 08:20.690
I caused a great deal of trouble for you 
in the matter with Lady Euphyllia.

08:20.690 --> 08:23.280
I wanted to apologize formally.

08:23.280 --> 08:26.110
Why don't you apologize to <i>her</i>, then?

08:26.110 --> 08:29.390
W-Well, yes, of course... 
I'll be doing plenty of that later.

08:32.090 --> 08:36.840
The truth is, I was the one 
who proposed this lecture.

08:36.840 --> 08:39.920
I hoped it would create an opportunity 
to restore your reputation.

08:39.920 --> 08:44.470
Wait, that was your idea? 
Not the Ministry's?

08:44.470 --> 08:47.760
Yes, so that you could do us 
the favor of teaching us

08:47.760 --> 08:51.220
about your magicology, an art that 
was unappreciated until now.

08:51.490 --> 08:54.120
I had hoped that could serve as my apology.

08:54.120 --> 08:55.510
R-Right...

08:55.870 --> 08:58.000
<i>I have no idea what he's talking about.</i>

08:58.000 --> 08:59.230
<i>What a weirdo.</i>

09:00.700 --> 09:04.430
I have no opinion on the matter. 
There's no need to apologize to me.

09:04.430 --> 09:07.180
But my conscience cannot accept that!

09:07.180 --> 09:10.910
Please hear me out for another 
ten minutes—no, an hour—

09:10.910 --> 09:14.120
no, for eternity, if that's what 
it takes to earn your forgiveness!

09:14.120 --> 09:16.330
<i>Huh? Is he a drunkard, too?</i>

09:22.660 --> 09:25.880
Please excuse me. 
I need to go talk to my friend.

09:25.880 --> 09:28.340
Your Highness's friend?

09:28.340 --> 09:30.830
Please introduce me to them, as well!

09:31.190 --> 09:34.810
And then we can all hear my father speak! Okay?

09:34.810 --> 09:37.250
Yes! Let's do that!

09:38.990 --> 09:39.930
In short...

09:39.930 --> 09:43.030
Only descendants of the king who 
made a contract with the spirits,

09:43.030 --> 09:48.130
meaning those who can use magic, 
have the right to rule this kingdom!

09:48.130 --> 09:50.470
Regardless of how many sophistries 
you may present us,

09:50.470 --> 09:54.350
we will never acknowledge a heretic 
who is incompatible with the spirits!

09:54.350 --> 09:57.810
<i>He's making no sense! 
I'm scared! What's his deal?!</i>

09:55.040 --> 09:58.440
To tarnish our traditions 
is to insult our kingdom!

10:00.620 --> 10:01.550
Ilia!

10:07.870 --> 10:09.820
Hey. Let go of me.

10:09.820 --> 10:12.590
Get everyone in the venue together! 
Don't let anyone leave!

10:15.250 --> 10:16.810
I said let me go!

10:16.810 --> 10:18.200
I can't do that!

10:18.200 --> 10:21.220
Until we know what that sound was, 
we cannot be imprud—

10:21.220 --> 10:23.720
That sound was an alarm that I invented!

10:23.720 --> 10:25.430
Something's happened at the villa!

10:27.960 --> 10:29.590
All the more reason.

10:29.590 --> 10:30.600
What?

10:30.810 --> 10:33.360
No, Your Highness!

10:33.360 --> 10:37.430
Please, calm yourself! Be rational!

10:37.430 --> 10:38.560
What are you—

10:38.560 --> 10:39.140
She's deranged!

10:39.540 --> 10:42.140
Princess Anisphia has lost her mind!

10:42.140 --> 10:44.080
Someone... Someone come help!

10:44.420 --> 10:45.540
What?

10:45.540 --> 10:48.760
I had a feeling this would happen someday,

10:48.760 --> 10:51.670
and I was right! You are a bizarre, 
dangerous individual!

10:51.670 --> 10:54.010
You're on a rampage! 
Consumed by debauchery!

10:54.010 --> 10:56.690
Outrageously audacious and running rampant!

10:57.010 --> 11:00.460
Restrain the deranged princess 
and keep her in here!

10:59.350 --> 11:00.460
Who are you...

11:00.930 --> 11:02.930
calling "deranged"?!

11:12.530 --> 11:14.970
L-Let me go! Let me go!

11:14.970 --> 11:16.200
That's...

11:17.850 --> 11:20.030
<i>my</i> line!

11:25.260 --> 11:26.850
A d-dragon!

11:26.850 --> 11:28.650
Wh-What are you doing?!

11:29.260 --> 11:32.620
Restrain this monstrous princess at once!

11:35.840 --> 11:37.300
You...

11:38.290 --> 11:40.300
monster!

11:45.770 --> 11:48.900
E-Euphyllia!

11:48.900 --> 11:49.690
Miss Anis!

11:49.690 --> 11:51.400
The window nearest the villa!

11:55.420 --> 11:57.170
What's all this, now?

11:57.170 --> 12:00.210
You all seem to be having such a good time.

12:05.100 --> 12:06.230
Tilty!

12:07.150 --> 12:09.820
A revolt? Is this a revolt?

12:10.130 --> 12:13.530
If that's what it is, I'll take you on.

12:14.060 --> 12:17.580
So go even wilder, won't you?!

12:20.930 --> 12:23.630
Such skillful composite magic...

12:24.720 --> 12:28.100
You'd better get out of here quick, 
or I'll tie everyone up.

12:28.350 --> 12:31.050
What are you doing, Tilty, you idiot?

12:31.500 --> 12:33.200
Are <i>you</i> an idiot?!

12:33.200 --> 12:36.010
I'm telling you to leave things here to me!

12:37.690 --> 12:39.230
Just don't take it too far.

12:41.160 --> 12:42.180
Euphie!

12:42.180 --> 12:42.910
Right!

12:48.930 --> 12:50.730
Wind Cutter!

12:52.870 --> 12:53.790
Let's fly!

12:53.790 --> 12:54.680
Do it!

13:01.370 --> 13:02.930
Honestly...

13:03.380 --> 13:06.470
You'd better do things right, 
Anis, you idiot.

13:08.910 --> 13:12.240
Oh, you're still on your feet?

13:15.210 --> 13:17.470
No one asked you to get involved.

13:17.810 --> 13:19.770
Must <i>every</i> last one of you...

13:19.770 --> 13:22.190
keep ruining my plans?!

13:22.600 --> 13:27.110
You insolent little girls, 
and your disregard for our traditions!

13:34.570 --> 13:36.000
Euphie! Over there!

14:21.930 --> 14:25.900
No matter what I do or how I do it,

14:25.900 --> 14:29.710
must you always stand in my way...

14:34.520 --> 14:35.800
Sister?

14:45.220 --> 14:49.600
What in the world is the meaning 
of this, Prince Algard?

14:50.000 --> 14:51.820
Keep it down, Euphyllia.

14:56.300 --> 14:58.090
Miss... Anis...

14:58.720 --> 15:01.700
I'm... sorry...

15:01.700 --> 15:04.120
Don't apologize. Lainie!

15:04.500 --> 15:07.330
I-I...

15:07.330 --> 15:08.820
Hang in there.

15:08.820 --> 15:11.040
You'll be fine. Just stay with me.

15:11.980 --> 15:15.940
Prince Al... Magicite...

15:16.290 --> 15:18.710
I know. Leave the rest to me.

15:18.710 --> 15:19.620
Euphie!

15:28.000 --> 15:29.500
Look after them.

15:30.640 --> 15:33.770
I can help Ilia, but Lainie...

15:33.770 --> 15:36.770
Lainie is a vampire. 
She still has a chance.

15:36.770 --> 15:40.310
But she's clearly had her 
magicite ripped out!

15:40.310 --> 15:43.200
Still, do everything you can. Please.

15:50.610 --> 15:52.490
Finished talking?

15:52.490 --> 15:54.860
How noble of you to wait for me.

15:54.860 --> 15:56.710
I'm used to waiting.

15:57.380 --> 16:00.310
I waited years for this moment, after all.

16:00.580 --> 16:04.520
Were you the one behind the 
lecture event at the Ministry?

16:05.490 --> 16:07.950
Wasn't that Moritz's idea?

16:08.470 --> 16:11.570
To get me away from the villa, yes.

16:11.570 --> 16:14.210
If you had the backing of the Ministry,

16:14.210 --> 16:17.300
that must mean its leader, Chartreuse, 
was working with you, too.

16:17.890 --> 16:18.700
Was he, now?

16:18.990 --> 16:23.170
I'm amazed you could do all that 
even under Lainie's fascination.

16:23.170 --> 16:28.370
I still hold her in the 
highest regard, of course.

16:28.670 --> 16:30.760
And what of it?

16:32.850 --> 16:38.560
Royalty should never let their emotions
lead them into poor decisions.

16:38.560 --> 16:41.000
That's been drilled into me all my life,

16:41.000 --> 16:43.590
as the one and only heir to the throne.

16:44.520 --> 16:47.940
So you'd just take Lainie's magicite 
from her without a second thought?

16:47.940 --> 16:50.330
Yes. My emotions are secondary.

16:50.640 --> 16:54.870
And you think becoming a vampire 
is the right thing for royalty to do?!

16:54.870 --> 16:57.250
You're the last one 
I want to hear that from.

16:57.910 --> 17:00.870
What is that on your back, pray tell?

17:01.790 --> 17:04.120
You may not have absorbed 
the magicite in the same way,

17:04.120 --> 17:07.860
but we both sought the powers of monsters—
a vampire and a dragon—

17:07.860 --> 17:09.530
just the same.

17:10.030 --> 17:13.360
You and I are in very different positions.

17:15.550 --> 17:16.610
That's right!

17:16.610 --> 17:19.740
You're a princess who threw away your 
right to the throne like it was nothing,

17:19.740 --> 17:22.770
and I'm the one and only crown prince 
who was left behind!

17:23.140 --> 17:24.850
Our positions <i>are</i> different!

17:25.230 --> 17:26.300
Al...

17:26.810 --> 17:29.620
That's why I had no choice but to do this.

17:30.110 --> 17:35.040
I will use the power of a vampire 
to seize control of this kingdom.

17:35.040 --> 17:36.740
Seize control?

17:37.240 --> 17:41.990
But why?! You'd still be the next king, 
even if you hadn't done that!

17:41.990 --> 17:46.760
If you sincerely believe that, 
you really have been oblivious.

17:47.480 --> 17:52.200
How many people have truly 
accepted me as the next king?

17:52.790 --> 17:55.370
You can't tell me you haven't 
heard people saying,

17:55.370 --> 18:00.520
"If only Princess Anisphia 
had a talent for magic"!

18:01.180 --> 18:05.330
Everyone acknowledges you, 
ridicules you, and fears you.

18:05.840 --> 18:09.290
You are genuinely a monster.

18:09.290 --> 18:10.160
You're wrong.

18:10.630 --> 18:13.440
No ordinary human can 
match up to a monster.

18:13.440 --> 18:15.870
So I have no choice but to become one!

18:15.870 --> 18:18.110
If there's no other way, then so be it!

18:18.110 --> 18:21.830
You're wrong! That's not the kind of king 
people want you to be!

18:22.560 --> 18:25.150
Can't you just treasure the ties 
that bind people to each other,

18:25.150 --> 18:29.040
and be a king who works hand-in-hand 
with them to lead the kingdom?!

18:29.040 --> 18:31.760
A king like that can only 
be called ornamental!

18:33.220 --> 18:36.490
The ties that bind people? 
Working hand-in-hand?

18:37.000 --> 18:39.460
Well, I... I've seen it!

18:39.800 --> 18:42.640
The rifts that gape between 
commoner and commoner!

18:42.660 --> 18:46.670
The arrogance of nobles who don't 
even see commoners as people!

18:46.670 --> 18:49.670
In this kingdom, magic is everything!

18:50.100 --> 18:53.660
Which is why you should be 
a king who changes that!

18:53.660 --> 18:54.890
It can't be changed!

18:54.890 --> 18:57.120
What happened when the previous king

18:57.120 --> 19:00.460
extolled commoners 
and gave them noble titles?!

19:02.230 --> 19:03.810
A revolt!

19:03.810 --> 19:05.950
One that involved many of the nobles!

19:06.370 --> 19:09.460
Even now, after Father and Duke put it down,

19:09.460 --> 19:11.920
its flames still smolder!

19:14.630 --> 19:16.950
This kingdom is ill.

19:16.950 --> 19:20.100
So I have no choice but to change it 
with absolute power.

19:20.100 --> 19:23.320
Power great enough to shatter 
the unchangeable norm.

19:24.640 --> 19:25.510
But...

19:26.620 --> 19:28.190
I couldn't do it.

19:29.570 --> 19:30.930
Al?

19:31.330 --> 19:34.130
I'm a foolish commoner 
who doesn't even compare to you.

19:34.580 --> 19:37.710
I couldn't excel in anything. 
I could do nothing.

19:37.710 --> 19:39.930
No matter how hard I tried,

19:39.930 --> 19:43.140
all I could do was things that were 
possible if I just worked at them.

19:43.480 --> 19:47.870
And that's why you sought power, 
even if you had to steal it?

19:47.870 --> 19:52.000
It's power that is necessary 
to correct this misguided kingdom.

19:52.380 --> 19:56.700
And you have no right to say 
a single thing about it.

19:57.300 --> 19:59.560
Anisphia Wynn Palettia.

20:00.000 --> 20:02.010
You are the first princess,

20:02.010 --> 20:04.960
and you threw away the responsibilities 
burned into that name.

20:05.780 --> 20:08.790
This is the future you chose not to pursue.

20:08.790 --> 20:12.010
If it's something a monster 
could throw away so easily,

20:12.010 --> 20:15.040
what problem is there with a foolish 
commoner like me vomiting blood

20:15.040 --> 20:16.770
for the chance to pick it up?

20:16.770 --> 20:20.030
Al, tell me one thing.

20:20.030 --> 20:22.110
What is magic to you?

20:22.110 --> 20:24.710
It's a curse, Sister.

20:26.660 --> 20:30.930
Magic, the royal blood, 
my position as a prince...

20:31.300 --> 20:33.410
To me, they're all curses.

20:33.940 --> 20:37.510
They're meant to reduce me to nothing.

20:38.720 --> 20:39.820
I see.

20:40.730 --> 20:43.130
Fine, Algard.

20:43.130 --> 20:47.610
Maybe the place where you stand right now 
is something I threw away.

20:48.320 --> 20:50.760
But I can't allow that.

20:51.200 --> 20:54.840
If you're going to pick up the 
future that I threw away,

20:55.550 --> 20:58.450
then I'll pick up the present 
that <i>you</i> just threw away.

20:59.220 --> 21:01.810
A kingdom ruled by an inhumane king

21:01.810 --> 21:03.610
who hurts people and 
tramples them underfoot

21:04.140 --> 21:06.060
is not a kingdom where 
people can live happily.

21:06.060 --> 21:10.020
None are more unfortunate than a people 
ruled by a king who lacks power!

21:10.020 --> 21:13.410
Power? How very comical.

21:13.410 --> 21:16.760
Are you really so vain as 
to believe you can beat me

21:17.230 --> 21:19.210
when we fight on equal ground?!

21:19.840 --> 21:22.420
How dare you?!

21:22.770 --> 21:24.870
If power really is everything,

21:24.870 --> 21:26.940
then let's see you beat me!

21:26.940 --> 21:31.640
I told you that you do not have 
the right to stand in my way!

21:31.830 --> 21:34.890
No. I will stop my brother's little game.

21:34.890 --> 21:36.850
That's my right as your older sister!

21:37.180 --> 21:40.050
It's too late for that nonsense now!

21:40.720 --> 21:44.290
Yes, it really is... too late.

21:45.240 --> 21:46.270
But, you know...

21:46.710 --> 21:48.900
Magic is made up of prayers for tomorrow

21:48.900 --> 21:52.950
and wishes for everyone's happiness, Al.

21:53.320 --> 21:54.490
Sister...

21:55.400 --> 21:57.780
Face me, Algard!

21:58.210 --> 22:01.270
I reject your definition!

22:02.000 --> 22:05.010
Episode Eight







The Magic Definition of the 
Monster and the Commoner

23:35.010 --> 23:40.010
Episode Nine







The Sister and Brother, and for 
Whom the Crown Is Intended
